# Prometheus Swarm CLI — Complete Redesign

A complete, end-to-end CLI system inspired by Claude Code and Cursor, designed to make every agent's inner workings **visible, trustworthy, and beautiful**. When approved, this plan replaces the existing rendering pipeline with a unified, scroll-based streaming architecture.

---

## The Core Philosophy

> **"Autonomy is legible."** — Every state the user sees must be real, every transition must be earned by an actual backend event, and the streaming must feel alive — like watching a brilliant team work in real time.

The current system has **two competing renderers** ([unified_live.py](file:///c:/Users/moham/OneDrive/Desktop/prometheus-swarm/prometheus/ui/claude/unified_live.py) and [live_tree.py](file:///c:/Users/moham/OneDrive/Desktop/prometheus-swarm/prometheus/ui/claude/live_tree.py)) that fight for the same job. The new design unifies everything into a single, scroll-based streaming renderer that prints content **once and scrolls down** — exactly like Claude Code and Cursor do. No `rich.Live` screen rewriting. No flickering. Just smooth, permanent output that the user can scroll back through.

